- 2 cans (400 g / 14 oz each) black-eyed peas, drained and rinsed
- 2 ripe plantains, peeled and sliced diagonally
- 3 tablespoons red palm oil, or vegetable oil
- 1 medium onion, finely chopped
- 1 can (400 g / 14 oz) chopped tomatoes
- 1 tablespoon tomato paste
- 1 garlic clove, minced
- ½ teaspoon chili flakes, or to taste
- Salt and black pepper
- Oil for frying the plantain
- Optional: gari for serving
Method
1. Heat the palm oil in a pot over medium heat. Add the onion and cook until soft, about 5 minutes.
2. Stir in the garlic and tomato paste; cook for 1 minute. Add the tomatoes, chili, salt, and pepper. Simmer for 10–15 minutes until the sauce thickens.
3. Fold in the black-eyed peas and a splash of water. Simmer for 10 minutes, stirring gently, until hot and saucy.
4. Meanwhile, heat a thin layer of frying oil in a pan. Fry the plantain slices for 2–3 minutes per side until golden and tender. Drain on paper towel.
5. Serve the bean stew with fried plantain and gari, if you like.
